                            <comment id="15180674" author="vkulichenko" created="Fri, 4 Mar 2016 22:41:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;IgniteClientDisconnectedException&lt;/tt&gt; should also behave consistently, regardless of whether the client was reconnected within network timeout or after it with a new ID. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15186613" author="sboikov" created="Wed, 9 Mar 2016 06:31:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Now after client reconenct we check that cache still exists and have the same deploymentId (GridCacheProcessor.onReconnected). So even when client reconnects with new ID old caches should work if they were not re-created while client was disconnected. Maybe it can be improved and after reconnect we should ignore deploymentId, but check that cache have the same configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15309904" author="damaan" created="Wed, 1 Jun 2016 08:14:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The issue description refers to &quot;special logic&quot; but does not mention how this logic would be implemented. Is there a &quot;known workaround&quot; to this problem that users of Ignite 1.5.x can deploy?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
