                            <comment id="16198771" author="ilyak" created="Tue, 10 Oct 2017 14:50:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;When operation hits a closed cache proxy, instead of throwing exception we should try to retrieve cache with the same name from KernalContext.&lt;br/&gt;
If that it successful, we update internal state and serve the operation as if the cache is always open.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Obviously it means that there was a period of time when this cache object won&apos;t be valid, we&apos;re teaching bad habits a bit, but with common try-catch-wait-retry loops it should work OK.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
